---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import ArticleSchema from '../../components/ArticleSchema.astro';
import { site } from '../../content';
const path = '/for/high-aov';
const title = "Shopify cart recovery for high-value stores";
const desc = "Route unresolved purchase questions to the right person before automating incentives.";
---
<BaseLayout title={title} description={desc} site={site} path={path}>
<ArticleSchema title={title} description={desc} siteName={site.name} domain={site.domain} path={path} />
<section class="container py-16 md:py-24">
<a class="link" href="/for">← All store types</a>
<h1 class="hero-title mt-6">Shopify cart recovery for high-value stores</h1>
<p class="mt-7 max-w-3xl text-xl leading-9">Route unresolved purchase questions to the right person before automating incentives.</p>
<article class="prose-shopify mt-12 max-w-4xl">
<h2>Diagnose the decision barrier</h2>
<p>A large basket can reflect financing questions, installation requirements or a buyer comparing specifications. Provide the actual warranty, delivery and service terms for that item. Avoid treating an expensive cart as evidence that a buyer wants credit or should receive a discount. A consultation request should create an owned follow-up task with context.</p>
<h2>Give the salesperson and automation one owner</h2>
<p>Require the tool to distinguish an active quote, a scheduled consultation and an unattended checkout. Decide who pauses automated messages while a representative works with the buyer. A verbal acceptance or a draft quote is not necessarily a paid order; document which event ends reminders and which merely suspends them.</p>
<h2>Proposed acceptance exercise</h2>
<p>Start a checkout, request a consultation and assign a representative. Inspect whether the next automated reminder pauses and whether the rep can see the product configuration. Complete the order through the agreed assisted-sales route and check the purchase exit. Repeat when the consultation is canceled so suspended shoppers do not remain stranded indefinitely.</p>
<h2>Evaluate assistance and contribution</h2>
<p>Score candidate tools on configuration retention, task ownership and recoverable pause states. Use a clearly hypothetical $2,000 sale with $1,200 goods cost: full-price gross contribution is $800; a 10% revenue discount costs $200 and leaves $600 before service, shipping, payment and channel costs. Include assisted orders in analysis while keeping attribution distinct from evidence of incremental sales.</p>
<h2>Check the trigger before replacing the tool</h2>
<p>Shopify distinguishes checkout recovery from earlier cart activity. Review <a class="link" href="https://help.shopify.com/en/manual/promoting-marketing/create-marketing/abandoned-checkouts">Shopify’s recovery eligibility</a> and inspect the actual workflow before comparing replacements. Proposed exercises above have not been performed.</p>
<p>Related decisions: <a class="link" href="/for/digital-products">digital product shops</a> · <a class="link" href="/for/fashion">fashion stores</a>.</p>
</article>
</section>
</BaseLayout>
